      'The other way: the inner 3rd moves up first, and the outer voices (strings 5 and 2) follow it into the new chord. Four 8ths a chord: old inner 3rd, new inner 3rd, the new bass and top together, the new inner 3rd again.',
      '- From E–G (open G, D string 2nd fret: the inner 3rd of B♭–E–G–C♯) up to F–A, then B and D around it: that’s B–F–A–D',
      '- Then F–A to G–B♭ with C♯ and E outside, and on up the scale to B–F–A–D at the 14th fret',
