      'Four grips a bar, each from that chord’s scale of chords: Dm7 as F6-dim, G7 with E♭°7, Cmaj7 as C6-dim, Fmaj7 as F6-dim. The skill is the joins: the last grip of each bar is a step from the first of the next.',
      '- <b>Dm7</b>: D–A–C–F (x5756x), C♯–G–B♭–E, C–F–A–D (x3323x), then A–E♭–F♯–C on strings 6-3',
      '- <b>G7</b>: G–D–F–B (3534xx), A–E♭–F♯–C, B–F–G–D, then D–G♯–B–F on strings 5-2',
      '- <b>Cmaj7</b>: C–G–A–E (x3525x), D–G♯–B–F, E–A–C–G, C♯–G–B♭–E',
      '- <b>Fmaj7</b>: C–F–A–D, C♯–G–B♭–E, D–A–C–F, E–B♭–C♯–G on strings 4-1',
      'This is the ii–V–I–IV that opens “Autumn Leaves”. From the Guitar Luminary handout “Drop2 Common Progressions”.',
