      'The A section (| Am6 | Am6 | A♭°7 | A♭°7 | Gm7 | C7 | F°7 Fmaj7 | Fmaj7 |) with one scale of chords for each chord, drop 2 on strings 5-2, in order.',
      '- <b>Am6</b>: Am6-dim from A–F♯–C–E (open A string) up to F♯–C–E–A at the 9th fret',
      '- <b>A♭°7</b>: the E7 scale. The handout hears A♭°7 as a dominant leading back to A minor (G♯°7 is E7♭9), even though it comes after Am',
